  "AI content payment is not merely a copyright or transaction-efficiency problem; it is a question of political-economic legitimacy. As AI valuations reach hundreds of billions, society asks why the gains from public web content and human knowledge accrue to a few firms. The paper proposes a six-layer tiered data market — from free public content through scarce verified datasets to public benefit-sharing — and defines the AI network democratic economy: rights, pricing, participation, auditability, and returns, each democratized through machine-readable protocols like AICR/AICL.": "I apas blong AI kontenido, ti ha' un problema put kopiraet pat efisiensia blong transaksion; un kuestion este put lehitimidåt politikat-ekonómika. Taemanu i balen AI siha ma'a'chetton para sientos de bilion, i sosiedåt ha faisen pot hafa i ganansia siha, ni ginen i pabliko na web kontenido yan i tiningo'ta komo taotao, man ma'apåsi ha' gi didide' na kompaniña. I papet ha propone un maketan data gaige sais na nibet — desde fri na pabliko na kontenido, para dataset siha ni eskes yan berifikao, asta i komparte prubechu para publiko — yan ha difini i ekonomia demokrátika blong netwotk blong AI: diritchu, presiu, patisipasion, oditabilidåt, yan ginanansia, kada uno ma'demokratisa pot medio protokolo siha ni matatataitai ni måkina, taegüe'ni AICR/AICL.",
