  "Continue to site": "Sigi para i sitio",
  "Convert rights declarations into a workable licensing market instead of a binary open/closed web.": "Kombietti i deklarasion siha put diritchu para un maketan lisensia ni fuma'chocho', ti ha' un web binaria put mababa/ma tåpa'.",
  "Copied ✓": "Ma kopia ✓",
  "Copy": "Kopia",
  "Correct positioning: independent research drafts, protocol proposals, and an open specification experiment.": "Korekto na posision: boradot siha put estudio independiente, propuesta siha put protokolo, yan un eksperimento put espesifikasion ni ma baba.",
  "Corrected an earlier default: Belgium (BE) now maps to Dutch instead of French — Flemish speakers are the country’s majority (~60%) over Walloon French speakers (~40%).": "Ma korihi un defolt antes: Belgium (BE) pa'go ma dana' yan Fino' Dutch, ti Fino' Fransia — i man kuentos Flemish, mås dångkulo na parte (kasi 60%) gi ayu na nasion, ki i man kuentos Walloon French (kasi 40%).",
  "Corrected an earlier default: Kazakhstan (KZ) now maps to Kazakh instead of Russian, now that a Kazakh translation exists — the same kind of fix as the earlier Belgium correction.": "Ma korihi un defolt antes: Kazakhstan (KZ) pa'go ma dana' yan Fino' Kazakh, ti Fino' Rusia, pa'go na guaha un translasion gi Fino' Kazakh — mismo klasen korekshon yan i korekshon antes put Belgium.",
  "Could AI Be Conscious?": "Could AI Be Conscious?",
  "Crawler access rules": "Lai siha put akseso blong crawler",
  "Crawler simulator": "Simuladot blong crawler",
  "Currency": "Klasin Salåppe'",
  "Custom tier": "Nibet Kustomisao",
  "Daily Nous reports on a retracted Journal of Medical Ethics submission containing multiple fabricated, AI-hallucinated references — complete with fake university affiliations and defunct email addresses — that the author reportedly left uncorrected even after being given a chance to fix proofs. The piece contrasts this with Bioethics, whose automated reference-checking would have caught the problem, and argues the real bottleneck isn't detection technology (one commenter's script flagged the fake citations in under a minute) but unpaid reviewer labor and publishing incentives that reward throughput over scrutiny.": "I Daily Nous ha ripota put un dokumento na ma po'lo tåtte (retracted) gi Journal of Medical Ethics, ni gaige mumu na refetensia siha ni AI ha alusinaesta — kumpleto yan fatso na afiliasion universidåt yan email adress siha ni ti fuma'chocho' esta — ni i eskritot, akoding, ti ha korihi asta ki ma nå'e chansa para u korihi i pruf siha. I atikulo ha kompåra este yan Bioethics, ni i chumecha' otomatiko blong refetensia siha, bai u fuma'sodda' i problema; ha sostiene na i berdadero na bottleneck, ti i teknolohia put fuma'sodda' (un komentadot ha ripela un script yan ha fuma'sodda' i fatso na sitasion siha gi mås kinu un minuto), lao i mano'chocho' blong rebisadot siha ni ti ma'apåse, yan i insentibo siha put publikasion ni ma premia i kantidåt mås kinu i kuidåo.",
  "Data free-riding vs. trillion-dollar AI valuations": "Fina'usa Data Sin Apas kontra i Balen AI ni Rijim Trilion Dolat",
  "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI": "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI",
  "Demis Hassabis proposed a FINRA-style regulator for frontier model releases: labs would submit models for review up to 30 days before deployment, voluntary at first, with a path toward mandatory compliance in the US market.": "Si Demis Hassabis ha propone un regulador estilo FINRA para i rilis siha blong frontier moddelo: i lab siha bai u fanma'sumitte moddelo siha para rebision, asta 30 dias antes di deploya, boluntåryo fine'nana, yan un chalan para kumplimento ni mandatorio gi i maketan US.",
  "Denied": "Ti Mapetmite",
  "Deployable policy starter template": "Template para Tutuhon Polisi ni Siña Ma Deploya",
  "Deployable policy starter template at /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — a minimal static site with the full machine-readable layer, ready for Cloudflare Pages or any static host.": "Template para tutuhon polisi ni siña ma deploya, gi /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — un sitio estátiko minimo yan i fulwan na kapa ni matatataitai ni måkina, redi para Cloudflare Pages pat eni otro host estátiko.",
  "Deploying machine-readable policies on your site": "Fina'deploya polisi siha ni matatataitai ni måkina, gi sitio-mu",
  "Disclaimer": "Diskleimet",
  "Distinct from human UI, SEO, or plain APIs, the AI Ingestion & Capability Layer gives websites a machine-facing architecture: a Manifest Layer (entry points like /llms.txt and /ai/manifest.json), a Corpus Layer (machine-readable knowledge), a Capability Layer (agent-callable tools), and a Governance Layer (provenance, licensing, versioning). Static-first, upgradeable toward APIs and MCP. Note: in this paper AICL names the ingestion architecture; on this site's protocol pages AICL refers to the AI Content Licensing Layer.": "Diferente gi UI blong taotao, SEO, pat simple API, i AI Ingestion & Capability Layer ha nå'e i websitio siha un akitektura ni fuma'atan para måkina: un Kapan Manifest (puntan entrada taegüe'ni /llms.txt yan /ai/manifest.json), un Kapan Corpus (tiningo' ni matatataitai ni måkina), un Kapan Kapabilidåt (tul siha ni siña ma aggang ni ehente), yan un Kapan Fina'gobietna (orihen, lisensia, bersion). Estátiko fine'nana, siña ma apgreida para API yan MCP. Nota: gi este na papet, AICL i na'an blong i akitektura blong ingestion; gi i påhina siha put protokolo blong este na sitio, AICL ha referi para i Kapan Lisensian AI Kontenido.",
  "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm": "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm",
  "Docs": "Dokumento",
  "Docs / Examples": "Dokumento / Ehemplo",
  "Document library": "Laibreria blong Dokumento",
  "Does AI have rights — and which framings are even coherent?": "Guaha diritchu i AI — yan håfa na framing mismo makesensia?",
  "Download": "Daonlod",
  "Draft status": "Estao blong Boradot",
  "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026": "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026",
  "Educational demo: HMAC-SHA256 with a shared secret, showing request-bound, expiring, verifiable license tokens. Production tokens should be signed asymmetrically, with the publisher’s public key discoverable under /.well-known/.": "Demo para fumanå'gue: HMAC-SHA256 yan un sekreto ni ma comparte, ha fanuè'i token siha put lisensia ni ma amåtta gi finaisen (request-bound), gaige espirasion, yan siña ma beripika. I token siha put produksion debi di ma firma gi manera asimétriko, yan i pablik kii blong publikadot siña ma sodda' gi sanhalom /.well-known/.",
  "Eight more /topics entries, this time researched by an AI agent rather than curated by hand — same rule as before: every source fetched and confirmed live, summaries an original paraphrase, before anything gets added. 14 entries total.": "Ocho mås na entrada siha gi /topics, este biåhe un ehente AI fuma'estudia, ti ma kurada ni kannai — mismo lai yan antes: kada orihen ma konne' yan ma konfitma na ripela, i sumario siha un orihinåt na parafres, antes di eni na hafa ma adda. 14 na entrada gi tetatåt.",
  "Email": "Imet",
